=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# Note$
# Compare mode: each section shows the current pattern, as$
# hardn's components render it today (P-23, P-24; built), and$
# beside it or under it the proposed one (P-42): a mock after$
# Figma's rows, drawn by the gallery. No component changed.$
# Proposed: the subject at column 6 and its state, a coloured$
# word with no colon, in one column after it; notices as$
# callouts, neutral lines as muted prose.$
# Markers: the key-value bullet on every row, as here; Figma's$
# status markers take its place, for a step done, failed or$
# rolled back, with -marker status.$
# Status column: two cells after the widest title, as here; with$
# -column figma it is Figma's column 27, which these titles$
# reach, so their rows stack at every width.$
$
# compare success ----------------------------------------------$
$
# Current ------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Done: Install hardn's boot unit$
  [+] Done: ufw: allow 2230/tcp$
  [+] Done: Add SSH port 2230$
  [+] Done: Reload sshd (ssh.service)$
  [+] Done: sshd -T shows ports 22, 2230$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
  [ ] Warning: This change reverts automatically in 3:01$
      To keep it, open a new SSH session on port 2230 and run:$
      sudo hardn confirm$
$
  [i] Info: Unless confirmed, change 20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
      is rolled back at 12:03:01 UTC. To undo it now, run sudo$
      hardn rollback 20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx.$
$
# Proposed -----------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Install hardn's boot unit     Done$
   -  ufw: allow 2230/tcp           Done$
   -  Add SSH port 2230             Done$
   -  Reload sshd (ssh.service)     Done$
   -  sshd -T shows ports 22, 2230  Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
# Warning$
# This change reverts automatically in 3:01$
# To keep it, open a new SSH session on port 2230 and run:$
$
      $ sudo hardn confirm$
$
  Unless confirmed, change 20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx is rolled$
  back at 12:03:01 UTC. To undo it now, run sudo hardn rollback$
  20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx.$
$
$

